Eliminate the per-iteration OOB bounds check in
`_tilemap_render_uncached_full_loop`'s inner body when bbox-skip
clipping (slot 0113) is also active.

Mechanism. Factor the inner-loop body into a template
`_tilemap_inner_render_dispatch<bool bounds_known>` in the same
anonymous namespace. The function's outer dispatcher reads the
existing slot-0113 bbox-skip helper + the new slot-0128
`tile_bounds_skip_active()` helper:

  const bool bounds_skip_on = NXE::Diag::tile_bounds_skip_active();
  const bool dispatch_bounds_known = bbox_skip_on && bounds_skip_on;
  if (dispatch_bounds_known) _tilemap_inner_render_dispatch<true>(...);
  else                       _tilemap_inner_render_dispatch<false>(...);

Inside the template the bounds test is written as

  const bool in_bounds = bounds_known ||
      (((mapx + x) >= 0) && ((mapy + y) >= 0) &&
       ((mapx + x) < map.xsize) && ((mapy + y) < map.ysize));

Under `bounds_known=true` the literal-true short-circuits the OOB
compares (no side effects) and -O3 DCE's both the compare chain
and the `else { ++skipped_oob }` branch -- every iter of the
bounds-known variant skips four compares and three short-circuit
branches. Under `bounds_known=false` the original behavior is
preserved bit-for-bit.

Why a new killswitch instead of piggybacking on TILE_BBOX_SKIP.
TILE_BBOX_SKIP only clips the outer iteration range; the
inner-body OOB check is still essential for correctness in
the `=0` (default-OFF) path of slot 0113. Splitting the dispatch
on a second hint lets A/B iters measure the bounds-check-elim
gain in isolation (`SET SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_TILE_BOUNDS_SKIP=0`
keeps the bbox-skip but reverts to the bounds-checked variant --
no rebuild needed).

Defaults. `SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_TILE_BOUNDS_SKIP` is a default-ON
inverse-killswitch (mirror of patches 0088 / 0093 / 0117 / 0126's
strict-"0"-disables convention). Production env baseline already
has `TILE_BBOX_SKIP=1` per `realhw_bat_carry_production_baseline.md`,
so the production path is bounds-known + bbox-skip both engaged.

Wave-25 self-check invariant holds in both variants. In the
bounds-known variant `skipped_oob` stays 0 because no OOB iters
happen (the bbox-skip clipped range already excluded them at the
outer-loop level). In the bounds-checked variant the counter
bumps as before. Equation `visited == drawn_normal + drawn_special
+ skipped_attr + skipped_oob` therefore holds in both -- distinguish-
able by the skipped_oob field across A/B PLAYs.

Architectural classification. This is CPU-bound work (compares +
short-circuit branches in the inner loop, no memory-stride or
cache change). It survives wave-31's bandwidth-bound architectural
finding per `wave_17_4_partial_flush_regression.md` -- wave-31
refuted output-cache approaches because cache-blit-OUT bandwidth
equaled underlying-render bandwidth; slot 0128 doesn't change any
memory access pattern, just removes redundant compares.

Predicted savings. iter K slot-0111 instrumentation reported
visit_overhead = +6.7 us/tile x ~150 in-bounds tiles per FG/BG
flip ~ ~1 ms / flip total visit-overhead budget. The OOB compares
+ branch are ~30-50% of that budget (the remainder being array-
load + attribute-load + counter bumps which stay in the body).
Predicted -0.3 to -0.7 ms / flip; per `perf_predictions_unreliable.md`
predictions historically wrong 5-30x so wave-33 real-HW PODP-83
measurement is the essential gate. The broader brief predicted
-1 to -2 ms which would assume eliminating ~100% of visit_overhead;
my honest model says ~50% is the realistic ceiling.

Smoke. Builds clean at i486 -O3 -funroll-loops -fno-rtti. Binary
size delta -O3-comparable rebuild: ~+4 KB (two template
instantiations of the inner loop). No new -Wmaybe-uninitialized
or -Wstringop-overflow regressions vs the iter-N+5 (W32A1) build.
DOSBox-X smoke gate pending build-qa.

Files. Touches `src/graphics/Renderer.cpp` (new env helper
`_abl_tile_bounds_skip` + forward-decl + file-scope wrapper),
`src/Utils/diagnostic_timers.h` (forward-decl), `src/map.cpp`
(template helper + dispatcher in `_tilemap_render_uncached_full_loop`).
Out of map.cpp scope: BG-only callsites in `_tilemap_render_plain_-
tiles_into_cache` + `_tilemap_render_special_tiles_to_window` --
their bbox-skip / bounds-check footprint is different and a
separate slot if warranted.

Companion ride-alongs (not in this slot). The wave-32 revert of
patch 0127 (Lever B) is parked at `patches/nxengine-evo/_disabled/`
+ documented in `patches/nxengine-evo/_disabled/NOTES.md` (sibling
ride-along commit, separate slot). The CMakeLists.txt `-O3
-funroll-loops` working-tree edit is intentionally NOT in this
patch -- it predates slot 0128 and is tracked separately at the
team-lead's discretion (next-session hygiene: bake into a numbered
patch slot or leave as working-tree drift, team-lead call).
