+// && ((mapx+x) < map.xsize) && ((mapy+y) < map.ysize)` is dead-code-
+// eliminated by -O3 because the bbox-skip clipped range guarantees
+// in-bounds. When DISABLED (env=0), the bounds-checked variant is
+// used unconditionally -- preserves slot 0113 pre-H3 behavior exactly.
+//
+// Polarity: only literal "0" disables (mirror of patch 0088 / 0093 /
+// 0115 / 0117's killswitch convention). Any other value (unset, empty,
+// "1", "yes", garbage) keeps the bounds-known dispatch engaged. Cached
+// lambda + static const bool so the per-call dispatch guard is hoisted
+// at -O2.
+//
+// Engagement dependency: bounds_known dispatch fires ONLY when both
+// `_abl_tile_bbox_skip()` (slot 0113; production env-on) AND this
+// helper return true. If bbox-skip is off, the bounds-checked variant
+// runs (mapx+x may legitimately fall outside map; OOB check is load-
+// bearing for correctness in that path). This dependency is why the
+// dispatcher reads both helpers -- they are NOT independently toggleable
+// because the OOB check is only redundant under bbox-skip clipping.
+//
+// Predicted savings: -0.3 to -0.7 ms / flip (per iter K visit_overhead
+// = +6.7 us/tile x ~150 in-bounds tiles per FG/BG flip ~ ~1 ms/flip
